WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.783
Episode ten: when a run needs approval.

2
00:00:02.783 --> 00:00:06.565
This video assumes APEX installed, as in episode one.

3
00:00:06.565 --> 00:00:12.476
Run every command below from the APEX folder.

4
00:00:12.476 --> 00:00:28.492
A submission needs a person's approval when it may take more simulator runs, or start more runs, than the limits in service.toml ([approval] max_simulator_runs, 20,000 by default, and max_runs, 20).

5
00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:32.797
At a terminal, the command asks you, and your yes is the approval.

6
00:00:32.797 --> 00:00:40.910
Answer no, or submit from a script, and you get a pending token to approve instead.

7
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:52.388
To see it on a small run, lower the limit in your own services root's service.toml.

8
00:00:52.388 --> 00:01:05.524
The example's ES-MDA run may take 2,500 simulator runs, so it is now over the limit.

9
00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:06.430
We submit it.

10
00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.032
It asks before it runs.

11
00:01:08.032 --> 00:01:11.027
Answer y, and it is approved and submitted.

12
00:01:11.027 --> 00:01:27.210
Answer n, and you get the token; here we answer n.

13
00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:36.621
A token is bound to that submission and its cost, can be used once, and expires after 24 hours.

14
00:01:36.621 --> 00:01:40.063
Approve the token you were given, then submit again with it.

15
00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:51.565
Here we only type the command, with the page's example token; use your own.

16
00:01:51.565 --> 00:01:56.230
Then the same submission again, with --approval-token and your token.

17
00:01:56.230 --> 00:02:07.790
We only type it.

18
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:14.785
Remove the [approval] lines afterwards to go back to the default limits.

19
00:02:14.785 --> 00:02:21.317
Grants approve a budget in advance, for a client's experiment.

20
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:24.001
So: over the limits, APEX asks first.

21
00:02:24.001 --> 00:02:30.602
Your yes is the approval; no gives a pending token, which you approve and then submit with.

22
00:02:30.602 --> 00:02:37.438
Next, in episode eleven: the web UI and its AI assistant.

23
00:02:37.438 --> 00:02:42.938
Thank you for watching.
